+## 15. Endpoint inventory
+
+Two classes of route, and the distinction is load-bearing: **host-facing** routes are part of the
+contract a host integrates against and are covered by the conformance suite (§11); **control-plane**
+routes belong to the console and to onboarding, and a host never calls them.
+
+| Route | Class | Auth | Scope | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| `GET /v1/health` | operational | none | — | liveness/readiness; no auth by design |
+| `GET /v1/version` | operational | none | — | build identity; no auth by design |
+| `GET /v1/whoami` | **host-facing** | API key | any of `observe`, `decide`, `read_model`, `admin` | identity of the calling key; never returns key material |
+| `GET /v1/learners` | **host-facing** | API key | `observe` | the caller's learners only; `profile` and `date_of_birth` are decrypted on read |
+| `GET /v1/learners/{learner_id}` | **host-facing** | API key | `observe` | another tenant's id is `404 learner_unknown`, not 403 |
+| `POST /v1/learners` | **host-facing** | API key | `admin` | tenant comes from the key, never from the body |
+| `GET /v1/credits/balance` | **host-facing** | API key | `observe` | `available`, `held`, `consumed`, `forfeited`, `granted`; a query over grants, never a stored balance |
+| `POST /v1/admin/credits/grants` | **control-plane** | API key | `admin` | `201`; `Idempotency-Key` required (≥ 8 chars); a replay returns the original grant |
+| `POST /v1/admin/keys` | **control-plane** | API key | `admin` | excluded from §11; may only mint a subset of itself, never `admin` |
+| `POST /v1/admin/keys/{id}/revoke` | **control-plane** | API key | `admin` | excluded from §11; revocation is immediate and idempotent |
+| `POST /v1/admin/keys/{id}/expiry` | **control-plane** | API key | `admin` | excluded from §11; audited (`api_key_expiry_set`); a past timestamp is `422 payload_invalid` |
+
+**Reservations have no route.** Holding and settling credits moves money, and money moves on the
+engine's terms, not on a caller's: `reserve`, `settle` and `release` are engine-internal operations.
+There is no `POST /v1/credits/reservations`, and a request for one is `404 route_unknown` — not
+`405`, not `501`, because the route does not exist and saying otherwise would promise it.
+
+**The rule, stated once.** Everything under `/v1/admin/*` is control-plane: it requires the `admin`
+scope and is out of scope for the host-facing conformance list, because a host does not manage its
+own keys or buy credits — onboarding and billing do, and the console is where it happens.
+`/v1/whoami` is host-facing and stays: a host needs to know which key it is holding and when it
+expires, and that answer is not a capability, so any valid key may ask.
+
+Conformance check 1 (§11, "auth works; scopes enforced per endpoint") applies to the host-facing
+routes in this table and to nothing else. A conformance run that fails on `/v1/admin/*` is
+misconfigured, not a broken connection.
